---
import BlogPost from '../../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
import { LAST_CHECKED } from '../../data/site';

// Prices and calories come from each flavor's item page so the site stays consistent.
const ranking = [
  { name: 'Oreo Cookie', href: '/items/oreo-blizzard', small: '$4.49', cal: '420', why: 'The cookie pieces stay crunchy all the way down, and it never gets too sweet. It is the one we would order if we could only pick one.' },
  { name: 'Chocolate Chip Cookie Dough', href: '/items/cookie-dough-blizzard', small: '$4.49', cal: '590', why: 'Soft dough bites plus fudge. Rich, filling, and the closest thing to a sure bet after Oreo.' },
  { name: 'Turtle Pecan Cluster', href: '/items/turtle-pecan-blizzard', small: '$4.79', cal: '570', why: 'Salty pecans, caramel and chocolate. The best pick if you like sweet-and-salty.' },
  { name: 'Reese’s Peanut Butter Cup', href: '/items/reeses-blizzard', small: '$4.49', cal: '600', why: 'Big peanut butter flavor in every bite. Very rich, so a Small is plenty.' },
  { name: 'Choco Brownie Extreme', href: '/items/choco-brownie-blizzard', small: '$4.79', cal: '510', why: 'Brownie pieces, fudge and chocolate chunks. For people who want the most chocolate possible.' },
  { name: 'Heath', href: '/items/heath-blizzard', small: '$4.49', cal: '480', why: 'Buttery toffee bits that stay crisp. Underrated and a little less sweet than the candy-bar flavors.' },
  { name: 'Butterfinger', href: '/items/butterfinger-blizzard', small: '$4.49', cal: '470', why: 'Flaky peanut butter crunch. Good, but the pieces get chewy if you take your time.' },
  { name: 'Strawberry Cheesequake', href: '/items/strawberry-cheesequake-blizzard', small: '$4.79', cal: '520', why: 'Cheesecake bites and strawberry. Lighter tasting than the chocolate flavors.' },
  { name: 'M&M’s Milk Chocolate', href: '/items/mm-blizzard', small: '$4.49', cal: '490', why: 'Fun and colorful, but the candy shells freeze hard. Better for kids than for chocolate fans.' },
  { name: 'Cotton Candy (seasonal)', href: '/items/cotton-candy-blizzard', small: '$5.29', cal: '460', why: 'Bright and very sweet. Most adults will tap out halfway; kids love it.' },
];

const faqs = [
  { q: 'What is the best Blizzard flavor at Dairy Queen?', a: 'The Oreo Cookie Blizzard is the most popular flavor and our top pick. Cookie Dough and Turtle Pecan Cluster are close behind. A Small Oreo Blizzard typically costs about $4.49 and has 420 calories.' },
  { q: 'What is the most popular Blizzard flavor?', a: 'Oreo Cookie is Dairy Queen’s best-known and most-ordered Blizzard. It is on the menu year-round at every location.' },
  { q: 'Which Blizzard has the fewest calories?', a: 'Among year-round flavors, a Mini Butterfinger (about 290 calories) or Mini Oreo (about 300 calories) are the lightest choices. Calories roughly double from Mini to Medium.' },
  { q: 'How much does a Blizzard cost?', a: 'Most Blizzards cost about $3.49–$3.99 for a Mini, $4.49–$4.79 for a Small, $5.29–$5.79 for a Medium and $5.99–$6.49 for a Large. Seasonal and Royal flavors cost more. Prices vary by location.' },
];
---
<BlogPost
  title="Best Dairy Queen Blizzard Flavors, Ranked (2026)"
  description="Our ranking of the best Dairy Queen Blizzard flavors, from Oreo to Turtle Pecan, with typical prices, calories and which size to order."
  h1="Best Dairy Queen Blizzard Flavors, Ranked"
  crumb="Best Blizzard Flavors"
  eyebrow="Blizzard rankings"
  image="/Images/blog-blizzard-flavors.webp"
  imageAlt="Oreo Blizzard from Dairy Queen in a cup with a red spoon"
  datePublished="2026-01-15"
  faqs={faqs}
>
      <p class="lead"><strong>The best Blizzard at Dairy Queen is the Oreo Cookie Blizzard</strong>, followed by Chocolate Chip Cookie Dough and Turtle Pecan Cluster. A Small Oreo Blizzard usually costs around $4.49 and has 420 calories. Below is our full ranking of the year-round and seasonal flavors, with what each one tastes like and what you will pay.</p>

      <p>This is an opinion piece. We ranked flavors on three simple things: whether the mix-ins stay good from the first spoonful to the last, whether the flavor gets tiring before you finish, and value for the price. Your favorite might be different, and that is fine.</p>

      <h2 id="ranking">Our Blizzard ranking at a glance</h2>
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table class="size-table">
          <thead><tr><th>#</th><th>Flavor</th><th>Small price</th><th>Small calories</th><th>Why it ranks here</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            {ranking.map((r, i) => (
              <tr>
                <td><strong>{i + 1}</strong></td>
                <td><strong><a href={r.href}>{r.name}</a></strong></td>
                <td class="price-cell">{r.small}</td>
                <td>{r.cal}</td>
                <td>{r.why}</td>
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p style="font-size:.88rem;color:var(--color-text-muted);">Typical price; varies by location. Last checked {LAST_CHECKED}.</p>

      <h2 id="top-three">Why Oreo, Cookie Dough and Turtle Pecan win</h2>
      <h3>1. Oreo Cookie Blizzard</h3>
      <p>The <a href="/items/oreo-blizzard">Oreo Blizzard</a> has been on the menu since 1985 for a reason. The cookie pieces soften a little but keep their crunch, and the chocolate cookie balances the sweet vanilla soft serve. It works in any size: about 300 calories as a Mini, 420 as a Small. If you want a twist, the <a href="/items/royal-oreo-blizzard">Royal Oreo</a> adds a fudge-filled center for about 50 cents more.</p>

      <h3>2. Chocolate Chip Cookie Dough Blizzard</h3>
      <p>The <a href="/items/cookie-dough-blizzard">Cookie Dough Blizzard</a> is soft and chewy where Oreo is crunchy. The dough bites stay soft even when frozen, and the fudge makes it feel like a full dessert. It is heavier, at 590 calories for a Small, so the Mini is a good call after a meal.</p>

      <h3>3. Turtle Pecan Cluster Blizzard</h3>
      <p>Pecans, caramel and chocolate give the <a href="/items/turtle-pecan-blizzard">Turtle Pecan Cluster</a> a salty edge that most Blizzards do not have. The nuts do not freeze rock hard the way candy does. If you find most Blizzards too sweet, start here.</p>

      <h2 id="chocolate-peanut-butter">Best picks for chocolate and peanut butter fans</h2>
      <p>For pure chocolate, get the <a href="/items/choco-brownie-blizzard">Choco Brownie Extreme</a>: brownie pieces, fudge and chocolate chunks. For peanut butter, the <a href="/items/reeses-blizzard">Reese’s Blizzard</a> is the obvious choice, and the <a href="/items/royal-reeses-blizzard">Royal Reese’s</a> adds a peanut butter center. Both are rich. A Medium Reese’s is around 830 calories, so many people share one or stick with a Small.</p>

      <h2 id="lower-ranked">Flavors that fall short (and who should still order them)</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/items/mm-blizzard">M&amp;M’s</a>: the candy shells freeze hard, so the chocolate inside does not melt into the soft serve. Kids usually do not mind.</li>
        <li><a href="/items/cotton-candy-blizzard">Cotton Candy</a>: very sweet and very bright. A seasonal treat for kids more than a regular order.</li>
        <li>Fruit-heavy Blizzards: fruit adds water, so these melt faster. Eat them right away.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="seasonal">Seasonal and limited-time Blizzards</h2>
      <p>Dairy Queen rotates a Blizzard of the Month and seasonal flavors throughout the year. Fall brings <a href="/items/pumpkin-pie-blizzard">Pumpkin Pie</a>, and winter adds <a href="/items/peppermint-bark-blizzard">Peppermint Bark</a>, <a href="/items/peppermint-hot-cocoa-blizzard">Peppermint Hot Cocoa</a> and the <a href="/items/frosted-sugar-cookie-blizzard">Frosted Sugar Cookie</a> Blizzard. Other limited runs include the <a href="/items/royal-new-york-cheesecake-blizzard">Royal New York Cheesecake</a>, <a href="/items/strawberry-cheesequake-blizzard">Strawberry CheeseQuake</a>, <a href="/items/confetti-cake-blizzard">Confetti Cake</a>, <a href="/items/banana-cream-pie-blizzard">Banana Cream Pie</a> and the spicy-sweet <a href="/items/swicy-pineapple-tajin-blizzard">Swicy Pineapple Tajín</a>. Seasonal Blizzards usually cost about a dollar more than core flavors. See every current flavor and price on our <a href="/categories/blizzard-treats">Blizzard menu</a>.</p>

      <h2 id="tips">Tips for ordering a better Blizzard</h2>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Go Mini to try a new flavor.</strong> It costs about a dollar less than a Small and tells you whether you like it.</li>
        <li><strong>Ask for extra mix-ins.</strong> Most stores will add more for a small charge.</li>
        <li><strong>Mix your own.</strong> You can ask for two mix-ins in one Blizzard. Oreo plus cookie dough is a favorite. Our <a href="/blog/dairy-queen-secret-menu">DQ secret menu guide</a> has more combinations.</li>
        <li><strong>Use the DQ app.</strong> App deals often include Blizzard offers. See our <a href="/blog/dairy-queen-app-rewards-hacks">DQ app rewards guide</a>.</li>
      </ol>
  <Fragment slot="after">
      <div style="margin-top:40px;padding:24px;background:#FFFFFF;border-radius:16px;border:1px solid #EADBCA;text-align:center;">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Playfair Display', serif;font-size:1.8rem;color:#0B1E38;margin-bottom:8px;">See every Blizzard flavor and price</h3>
        <p style="color:#64748B;font-size:0.95rem;margin-bottom:16px;">Sizes, calories and typical prices for the full Blizzard menu.</p>
        <div style="display:flex;justify-content:center;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;">
          <a href="/categories/blizzard-treats" class="btn btn-primary">Blizzard menu and prices →</a>
          <a href="/categories/dq-cakes" class="btn btn-accent">Blizzard cakes →</a>
        </div>
      </div>
  </Fragment>
</BlogPost>
